  "intro": {
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Jared Taylor Isaacman (born February 11, 1983) is an American billionaire entrepreneur, pilot, and commercial astronaut who has served as the 15th administrator of NASA since December 2025. He founded the payment processor Shift4 Payments, which he led as chief executive until 2025, and co-founded Draken International, which provides adversary training to the U.S. and other air forces. Forbes estimated his net worth at US$1.5 billion as of April 2025.\nIsaacman commanded Inspiration4 – the first all-civilian spaceflight – using SpaceX's Crew Dragon Resilience, which launched from Kennedy Space Center on September 15, 2021. He later led Polaris Dawn, during which he became the first private citizen to perform a spacewalk.\nIn December 2024, President Donald Trump nominated him to serve as the 15th administrator of NASA. During his April 2025 confirmation hearing, Isaacman emphasized his outsider status and entrepreneurial background, stating his intent to usher in a \"new Golden Age of Science and Discovery\" at the agency. He faced questions over his close ties to Elon Musk, the founder of SpaceX, one of NASA's largest contractors. On May 31, 2025, Trump, among several actions preceding...",
    "sourceId": "wikipedia-en",
    "usage": "Research excerpt; paraphrase and cross-check before publication."
  },
